Once this is in place, the thing worth testing isn't each route — it's that no table with a mutating route lacks a trigger. A one-off query against `information_schema` (list audited tables from the trigger catalog vs. tables actually receiving `INSERT`/`UPDATE`/`DELETE` in the routes directory) run in CI catches the "added a new table, forgot the trigger" class of gap that route-by-route testing would miss.

