At 38k rows growing by a few hundred a month, a GIN-indexed Postgres query is sub-millisecond to low-single-digit-milliseconds — no need for Elasticsearch, Algolia, or Typesense. Those buy you things (synonyms, typo-correction out of the box, faceting at scale) this table doesn't need yet. Revisit only if the catalog grows by an order of magnitude or search becomes latency-critical at high QPS.

